A compact identity makes the logic clearer: $R_{\mathrm{trip}}
=
R_{\mathrm{lodging}}
+
R_{\mathrm{transport}}
+
R_{\mathrm{premium}}.$ This is not a spoken formula, but it preserves the mechanism faithfully. One guest, one trip, and several revenue surfaces, provided the offers solve consecutive needs rather than competing for the same attention.

